   236	
   237	## Notes for the reviewer
   238	
   239	* **What the health check can and cannot prove.** Two probes prove the reader can tell a
   240	  record from a non-record *at that moment*. They do not prove it will answer the next
   241	  question, which is why the unknown state exists as well: the health check is the cheap
   242	  catch for a reader that never fails but always lies, and the per-read unknown is the
   243	  catch for everything else. A regression exercises each separately (`always record` /
   244	  `always norecord` for the first, `fails on the trainer` for the second).
   245	* **Cost.** The health check adds two interpreter starts per scan and per resolution, on
   246	  a path that runs a handful of times per launch.
   247	* **`EXP11_PYTHON`** is the only new affordance, and it is inert outside
   248	  `EXP11_TEST_ROOTS=1` with `--dry-run`: any other invocation that sets it is refused
   249	  outright, which is itself regressed.
   250	* **A verdict that is not digits** is treated as unknown too (`2fc5300`): `kill -0 <word>`
   251	  fails, and a failed probe would otherwise read as "not alive". That case is healthy on
   252	  the probes, so only the per-read check catches it.
